    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. The version number and date (2026-10-20) come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files, and the entry follows the format of the earlier ones:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n- **Breaking change:** ACME-421 is marked `!` in the PR list, so I put it first and labelled it \"BREAKING\". That's a breaking change in a minor release (2.3.0 → 2.4.0). If you follow semantic versioning, this should be 3.0.0 instead. I left `VERSION` unchanged, so that's your call.\n- **No author names:** I didn't include the PR authors (@mira, @jonas and so on) because earlier entries don't list them. I can add them if you'd like credits.",
